      "math_academy_id": "q-34980",
      "sequence_position": 4,
      "problem": "Consider the matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -7\\end{aligned}]$ and the vector $b=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ k\\end{aligned}].$ Find the value of $k$ such that $b\\in \\text{Null}(A).$",
      "worked_solution": "If $b\\in \\text{Null}(A),$ then we must have $Ab=0.$ Substituting the given information, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Ab & =0 \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}2 & -7\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ k\\end{aligned}] & =0 \\\\ -7k & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand for this equation, we obtain $k=0.$",
